/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 522 0 R
/E (Ethical Concern: Streetify processes and stores highly sensitive PII \(Personally Identifiable Information\), including users' home addresses, live GPS telemetry, and financial data.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 523 0 R
/E (Mitigation Strategy: We adopted a "Privacy by Design" approach. User passwords are cryptographically hashed using bcrypt prior to database insertion. Passenger identity is dynamically masked during the ride broadcast phase \(drivers only see coordinates, not passenger names\). Furthermore, we utilized secure, stateless JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\) for authentication to prevent session hijacking.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 77 0 R
/T (5.2 Security, System Integrity & Abuse Prevention)
/E (5.2 Security, System Integrity & Abuse Prevention)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 524 0 R
/E (Ethical Concern: Malicious users could exploit the system, or administrative staff could abuse their high-level privileges to view or alter sensitive user data.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (Mitigation Strategy: We implemented a strict Role-Based Access Control \(RBAC\) architecture. To prevent internal abuse, our system includes an immutable AUDIT_LOG entity \(mapped as a Weak Entity in our EER\). Every time a System Administrator suspends an account or a Customer Experience Officer issues a refund, the action, timestamp, and staff ID are permanently logged. Additionally, if an account is flagged and suspended, the system immediately revokes active JWT tokens, severing live WebSocket and API access instantly to protect the platform.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
